# Kertel .gitignore
# Every private entry below carries the reason it is private.
# Infra and lockfiles stay tracked on purpose: a reviewer must be able to
# reproduce the exact dependency graph and the exact run commands.

# --- Internal planning and operations docs -------------------------------
# These are the build's private thinking. They carry unshipped scope, cost
# ceilings, blast-radius notes, and decision lineage that would read as
# product claims to anyone outside the build. The public repo gets README.md,
# docs/RUNBOOK.md, docs/DECISIONS.md and .env.example instead.
PLAN.md
PLAN-*.md
*_PLAN.md
HACKATHON_RESEARCH.md
docs/HACKATHON_AUDIT_*.md
docs/HACKATHON_AUDIT_*.evidence.json
docs/HACKATHON_CORE_PROBLEM_RESEARCH_*.md
docs/IMPLEMENTATION_*.md
docs/internal/
todo.md
TODO.md
demo_guide.md
docs/OPERATIONS.md
docs/feedback.md
notes/
scratch/

# --- Agent and assistant workspaces --------------------------------------
# Per-machine tooling config for whichever assistant the operator drives this
# from. It names local MCP endpoints and paths, is not part of the product, and
# would go stale the moment somebody clones this on a different machine.
.codex/
.claude/
.cursor/
.windsurf/
.aider*
.playwright-mcp/
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md

# --- Secrets --------------------------------------------------------------
# Never tracked. .env.example is tracked and holds names and comments only.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
.secrets/

# --- Local state ----------------------------------------------------------
# SQLite holds audit metadata and hashes for this operator's runs only.
# It is machine state, not source, and it must be restorable from a backup
# rather than from git.
data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# --- Generated output -----------------------------------------------------
# Evidence is generated by tracked scripts, never captured by hand. The
# recipe is committed, the output is not.
dist/
build/
out/
coverage/
.artifacts/
proof-output/
demo-output/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Dependencies and tooling caches -------------------------------------
node_modules/
.npm/
.pnpm-store/
.turbo/
.cache/

# --- Logs -----------------------------------------------------------------
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# --- OS and editor noise --------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# Next.js build output
web/.next/
web/node_modules/
web/out/
